From: Isaac Reed <imrisaac@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci: initialize after deferred probing

psci-cpuidle is a faux device, which probes synchronously from
faux_device_create() and cannot return -EPROBE_DEFER. In OSI mode each
CPU attaches to its PSCI PM domain, and on QCM2290 those domains are
only registered once their parent, the MPM, has probed. At
device_initcall time that has not happened yet: the attach fails,
faux_device_create() returns NULL and cpuidle is never enabled, leaving
the CPUs in WFI only.

  CPUidle PSCI: CPU 0 failed to PSCI idle
  CPUidle PSCI: Failed to create psci-cpuidle device
  CPUidle PSCI: Initialized CPU PM domain topology using OSI mode

Register the device at late_initcall_sync, after deferred probing has
been flushed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -489,4 +489,9 @@

 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+/*
+ * The faux device probes synchronously and cannot defer. In OSI mode the CPU
+ * PM domains may only be registered once their parent domain (e.g. the
+ * Qualcomm MPM) has probed, so wait until deferred probing has been flushed.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
